WEBVTT

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.310
Wh-what’s going on?!

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:14.360
Raetsel!

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.250
Raetsel!

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:26.920
Wh-where am I?

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.880
So you’ve finally arrived,

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:30.980
Kaito.

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:35.330
Raetsel!

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.910
It’s Insanely Fun to be Alive

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.190
Is this another past?

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:21.200
I see. I take it this is
the last barrier, Orpheus.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.710
Come on! It’s time we got started.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.760
Started? On what?

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:27.910
Chickening out?

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:30.210
Isn’t it obvious that I was referring
to the Puzzle of God?

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:31.830
The Puzzle of God?!

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:33.990
Jin and Count Pythagoras are

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:36.760
going to challenge the Puzzle
of God here tomorrow.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.340
But I could not possibly let Jin do
something that dangerous.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:44.220
So you want to solve it in his stead?

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:49.230
Right, even if that means
one of us could die.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:50.880
What should I do?

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.700
How can I bring back the old Raetsel?

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:56.980
Come on! Face me in a duel, Kaito.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:59.830
How can I get us out of this maze...?

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:02.490
You two! What are you doing here?

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:07.010
This is a dangerous puzzle that
could potentially take lives!

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:10.040
You shouldn’t be anywhere near here.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.040
Nonoha?!

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:14.620
Huh? Kaito? Are you Kaito?

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:16.640
Dude, what’re you doin’ here?

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:17.800
Right back at you, Kaito!

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:22.180
By any chance, have you kept our promise?

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:25.620
Kaito, have you continued to solve puzzles?

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:27.170
Promise...?

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:28.780
What promise are you--

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:37.570
I swear that I’ll be great at solving
puzzles by the next time I see you!

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:38.890
So...

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:44.070
Yeah! Let’s solve the hardest
puzzle in the world together.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:45.750
It’s a promise!

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:48.420
I’m holding you to this promise!

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:50.380
I see...

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:55.710
Challenge harder and harder puzzles
and solve them on your own!

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.980
You’ll have loads more fun that way!

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:03.220
Even I wish I could change part of my past.

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:06.780
I’ve continued to solve puzzles ever since.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.240
Now I’m a Solver working for the POG.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.870
Is that what brought you here?

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:16.370
I’m constantly traveling around,
solving puzzles across the world.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:20.610
I figured that in doing
so, I might run into you.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:25.630
Now let’s fulfill that promise and
solve the Puzzle of God together.

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:26.490
Together?

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:29.420
You can’t solve the
Puzzle of God by yourself.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:31.570
I was searching for a partner anyway!

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:33.250
Stop right there!

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:36.500
Who do you think you are,
butting in like this?

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:39.000
By any chance, are you Raetsel?

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:42.270
This battle is between the two of us.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:45.980
I have to defeat Kaito Daimon!

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:49.510
But... but you can’t
solve the puzzle like that!

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.740
Puzzles are filled with
a wide array of emotions.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:55.910
They hold the emotions of the
people who made them...

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.810
and the emotions of the
people who solve them.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:02.580
When a person solves a puzzle,
they’re always with someone else.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:06.030
They’re with the feelings of another...

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:10.200
The Puzzle of God is the
hardest puzzle in the world.

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:12.430
This is such a treat!

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:15.650
Let’s enjoy solving it together,
just you, Raetsel, Kaito and I!

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.470
Everyone, together...

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:21.920
Puzzle time... Let’s begin!

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:28.780
Huh? What’s this?

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:31.430
Thank you, Nonoha!

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:35.350
Let’s be sure to solve some
puzzles together sometime!

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:36.600
Kaito!

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:38.430
What’s going on?!

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:40.420
It’s a promise.

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:49.460
Where is this...?

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:55.850
Whatcha think of that?!
We escaped your Time Maze, Orpheus!

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:59.750
I would expect no less from my vessels.

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:04.210
I get it!

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:05.900
This is a puzzle where we
steal each other’s territory.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:08.510
The real puzzle has just begun!

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:11.570
Let’s enjoy it, Kaito Daimon!

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:14.190
Yeah! Puzzle time...

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:15.520
Let’s begin!

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:22.280
This strategy game uses the tower’s panels.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:26.580
I’m red. Kaito’s blue.

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:31.460
I can move four spaces vertically or
horizontally from where I’m standing.

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:33.960
A diagonal line will extend
from where I started,

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:37.200
connecting that panel to my current location.

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:41.970
That series of panels constitutes
my “territory.”

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:45.850
However, I’m not allowed to cross
over my own panels.

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:50.230
I can cross over my opponent’s
line to sever it.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:54.460
I get to keep the longer
of the severed lines.

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:57.600
If they’re the same
length, I get to keep both.

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:00.410
I can’t return to a panel I’ve
already selected once.

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:03.440
Same for panels that I’ve already claimed.

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:13.320
If I can’t move, I’ll have to skip
my turn until I can move again.

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:22.640
He’s pushing me up!

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:31.590
As things are now, I can’t win!

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:38.280
I’m going to enjoy this puzzle,
but at this rate, Raetsel will...

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:42.650
Let’s solve the Puzzle of God together.

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.050
Together...

00:07:57.340 --> 00:07:58.370
Kaito?

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:04.000
Kaito!

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:11.780
Kaito... You’re tough!

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:17.150
Kaito Daimon is launching an
all-out assault against Raetsel!

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:25.620
I can see it! I can see
Kaito Daimon as he awakens!

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:31.220
It’s game over...

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:35.630
But I had fun.

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:38.500
This is the first time I’ve enjoyed
such a fulfilling puzzle.

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:43.080
Thank you, Kaito.

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:46.720
Please take care of Jin for me.

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:47.530
Pass!

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:52.390
Kaito has run out of panels?!

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:55.150
That is a trivial matter.

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:56.930
It will not sway the future.

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.490
He’s skipping his turn? That’s nuts!

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:04.200
Does this mean...?

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:13.810
Raetsel...

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:16.050
Is that right?

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:19.130
Is this really what you meant, Kaito?

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:24.580
She’s expanding her red territory?!

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:26.580
I need to go there next!

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:27.960
Blank panels?!

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:33.520
Did Kaito Daimon leave
blank panels for Raetsel?

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:37.320
Is the ultimate Phi-Brain mind being used

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:39.970
to lead his opponent to victory?!

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:43.070
That’s absurd! Why would he do that?

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:46.850
It’s beautiful! What a beautiful move!

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:49.930
But even if that’s what he’s going for,

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:52.610
he is still way ahead of her!

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:55.610
How far can I go? But--

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:57.110
Pass!

00:09:57.110 --> 00:09:58.450
He skipped his turn again?!

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:03.040
With this, victory’s mine!

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:13.310
What?!

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:17.350
We did it, Kaito!

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:20.760
I believed in you, Raetsel.

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:24.770
Orpheus, I’m the one who won!

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:29.350
But Kaito is the one who solved the puzzle!

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:32.220
What do you have to say about that, Orpheus?!

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.200
Wh-what’s happening?

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:43.030
What?! What on earth is going on?!

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:52.850
Lovushka! Lovushka!

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:54.340
Raetsel!

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:56.810
Lovushka!

00:10:58.770 --> 00:10:59.800
Enigma!

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:05.260
Lovushka! Lovushka!

00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:22.800
You showed me something truly beautiful.

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:28.110
As a sign of my gratitude,
I shall spare your lives.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:29.740
However...

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:43.220
Kaito!

00:11:50.030 --> 00:11:51.600
The future is barely swaying.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:55.610
It is still in the palm of my hand.

00:11:58.540 --> 00:11:59.490
Kaito!

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:03.630
The time has come for me to enter your brain!

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:14.810
Kaito!

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:17.710
Kaito, pull yourself together!

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:24.190
Orpheus is entering Kaito’s mind...!

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:38.080
Kaito!

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:40.210
Jin!

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:57.770
Jin! Jin, hang in there!

00:12:57.770 --> 00:12:58.380
Jin!

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:06.990
I used the system that Cubik
invented to intercept Orpheus.

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:09.390
Rook, dude...!

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:10.890
You’re alive?

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:12.900
He couldn’t read my thoughts

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:15.250
when my mind was in
a state of confusion,

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:17.150
consumed by the Armlet.

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:21.590
Orpheus’ perception of the future swayed

00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:23.830
whenever something was related to Kaito.

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:27.890
That’s why I challenged
you to a puzzle battle

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:29.510
when I was consumed by the Armlet.

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:35.170
I tricked Orpheus into
thinking that I was dead and

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:36.420
waited for my chance to act.

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:38.320
I figured about as much!

00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:42.210
I thought you had some kind of plan.

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:44.800
I swear, he’s one impressive bastard!

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:48.930
It goes to show he had us
completely fooled, doesn’t it?

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:50.930
Gammon! Freecell!

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:54.820
Like that was enough to knock off Galileo,

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:56.830
the Great Gammon Sakanoue!

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:58.690
Or so I’d like to say, but...

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:01.070
Rook rescued us.

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:04.570
Yes. No one has been harmed.

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:03.750
Nonoha and the others
are also safe and sound.

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:06.880
We only had one chance.

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:10.090
We had to act the moment
Orpheus’ mind left Jin

00:14:10.090 --> 00:14:11.810
and tried to enter yours, Kaito.

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:13.990
We used those devises to block your mind.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:17.040
They prevented Orpheus from
transferring his mind into you or Jin.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:17.960
<i>Mission: Complete. Mission: Complete.</i>

00:14:18.220 --> 00:14:21.140
So Jin’s back to normal?

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:26.340
He’s not Jin!

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:27.470
What?!

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:32.600
The future... The future that I foresaw...

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:41.600
It changed?

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:47.580
Did we fail?

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:48.740
That can’t be right!

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:51.240
No, you didn’t actually fail.

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:55.710
You can hear us, can’t you?

00:14:56.150 --> 00:14:57.750
Come on out, Jin.

00:14:58.720 --> 00:15:02.380
Bastard! What do you mean by--Ngh!

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:11.190
Jin! Hang in there, Jin!

00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:14.610
S-stop it! Don’t!

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:17.020
Jin!

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:27.530
Jin...

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:28.780
Jin!

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:30.130
Huh?!

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:32.340
What the blazes is going on?!

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:36.660
Does this mean Orpheus didn’t
have control over Jin?!

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:41.920
Yeah. They had already merged together,
becoming one.

00:15:43.890 --> 00:15:49.630
When Orpheus nearly entered my
mind just a second ago, I felt him.

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:51.550
I sensed Jin with him.

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:53.190
That’s horrible!

00:15:53.190 --> 00:15:57.280
They reflected my heart and
bound me like chains...

00:15:57.570 --> 00:16:01.160
That is how I perceived puzzles.

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:03.810
They’re mirrors and chains...

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:07.230
I’m sure it must have
been the same for Orpheus.

00:16:08.120 --> 00:16:11.570
That’s probably why we synchronized.

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:16.940
But didn’t you tell us not to
challenge the Puzzle of God?

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:20.830
I don’t know... I just don’t know.

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:23.280
Where does my mind end...

00:16:24.070 --> 00:16:26.150
and Orpheus’ mind begin...?

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:27.310
What’s that supposed to mean?

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:33.480
Jin may have possessed the desire to
challenge the Puzzle of God as well.

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:38.100
He lost control of that desire
when it fused with Orpheus’.

00:16:38.570 --> 00:16:42.850
I was certain that you were capable
of becoming a Phi-Brain,

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:44.850
Kaito...

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:49.320
I thought that puzzles were
all that mattered to me,

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:52.800
but I was wrong...

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:55.300
In my heart,

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:59.240
I was constantly thinking about
how I needed to stop Pythagoras.

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:04.640
Raetsel, you said that you would do it for me,
but that’s the problem.

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:07.070
You must cast everything aside.

00:17:07.720 --> 00:17:12.140
Puzzles are the only
thing you can care about.

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:16.020
That will lead you to becoming a Phi-Brain.

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:20.440
I felt that the only one who
could reach such heights

00:17:21.230 --> 00:17:22.390
was you, Kaito...

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:26.850
That’s why you chose Kaito instead of me...

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:29.370
I don’t plan on castin’ anything aside.

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:37.290
A long time ago, I had the most fun
when I solved puzzles by myself.

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:39.660
I loved puzzles above all else.

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:43.000
But I’m different now.

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:45.800
’Course, there have been some hard times.

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:49.010
There have been sad times, painful times,

00:17:49.550 --> 00:17:52.760
and times I thought I hated puzzles.

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:56.110
But I was never alone.

00:17:56.980 --> 00:17:58.260
I’ve solved puzzles with everyone.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:00.760
Isn’t it strange?

00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:02.930
No matter how painful the puzzle was,

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:07.700
the moment I solved it,
it changed into a really fun memory.

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:12.090
Right now, solving puzzles with everyone

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:16.030
and living with them is insanely fun.

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:19.630
I could never throw that away!

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:24.820
It’s fun? That’s it!

00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:27.490
No matter what the situation,

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:30.500
you always remembered to have fun...

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:35.090
That is what makes a person truly strong.

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:36.670
It’s what I...

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:40.360
It’s what I was missing...

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:43.320
Raetsel,

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:47.210
I wanted you to cast puzzles aside

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:50.900
and enjoy a peaceful life.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:55.910
No matter what your intentions were,

00:18:56.550 --> 00:18:59.660
I’m happy that I met you.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.950
Thank you, Jin.

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:08.390
Kaito,

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:10.750
I’ll let you two be alone.

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:16.390
It’s my way of thanking you for
bringing the old Jin back.

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:23.900
Jin...!

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:27.430
Farewell!

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:42.130
Are you all right, Jin?

00:19:43.090 --> 00:19:48.830
I may have wanted this to happen...

00:19:49.760 --> 00:19:55.840
For you to stop Orpheus... to stop me...

00:19:58.100 --> 00:19:59.440
Kaito...

00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:04.730
I want you to make a puzzle.

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:09.360
I want to solve a puzzle with you...

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:14.080
It will be fun, just like the olden days...

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:15.480
Jin...

00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:00.040
Raetsel!

00:21:03.420 --> 00:21:05.780
Is this where you wanted it?

00:21:06.340 --> 00:21:07.450
Freecell!

00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:11.550
I’m sure everyone at school will be
shocked when they see this.

00:21:13.060 --> 00:21:13.790
Yeah.

00:21:14.970 --> 00:21:19.290
I want everyone to go all out and
have fun solving puzzles today.

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:22.800
Right. Today is the anniversary of Jin’s...

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:27.520
68th Graduation Ceremony at
Root Gakuen High School

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:41.710
Cubik, have you grown a bit taller?

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:44.070
Huh? You think I’m taller?

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:44.070
By 9.5mm. By 9.5mm.

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:46.340
What are you going to do now?

00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:47.400
Nothin’ much.

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:52.080
I’ll keep on makin’
and solvin’ puzzles. That’s all.

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:54.510
So how about you?

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:56.930
I will merely concentrate on my usual duties

00:21:56.930 --> 00:21:59.590
at the POG, working under Master Rook.

00:21:59.970 --> 00:22:02.160
How do you like studying art overseas?

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:04.340
Aren’t you studying in Paris?

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:07.410
Nuh-uh! N’Djamena!

00:22:08.190 --> 00:22:09.270
Where’s that...?

00:22:16.740 --> 00:22:19.100
I kept my word,

00:22:20.290 --> 00:22:21.100
Jin.

00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:27.740
It’s over. Everything is truly over.

00:22:29.880 --> 00:22:32.550
Nonoha, you still haven’t solved that?

00:22:32.720 --> 00:22:36.000
That’s the puzzle Kaito made for Jin.

00:22:36.430 --> 00:22:40.260
Didn’t you spend forever
working on that puzzle?

00:22:40.260 --> 00:22:43.060
What was with that “going on a journey
to perfect my skills” nonsense?!

00:22:43.060 --> 00:22:45.090
I can’t believe he left
without saying goodbye!

00:22:45.730 --> 00:22:48.810
He could have waited until after
the graduation ceremony!

00:22:49.400 --> 00:22:51.780
I wonder what he’s doing right now.

00:22:52.820 --> 00:22:54.730
You couldn’t solve a puzzle to save--

00:22:55.950 --> 00:22:57.870
I-I solved it!

00:22:58.740 --> 00:22:59.780
Nonoha...

00:22:59.780 --> 00:23:00.780
solved...

00:23:00.780 --> 00:23:02.770
a puzzle?!

00:23:04.830 --> 00:23:07.600
Jin, thank you very much!

00:23:10.880 --> 00:23:13.210
Hey, Nonoha! Where are you going?

00:23:13.420 --> 00:23:14.660
Isn’t that a given?

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:16.830
I’m going after Kaito!

00:23:17.180 --> 00:23:19.920
But we don’t know where Kaito is.

00:23:20.300 --> 00:23:22.010
It says right here!

00:23:22.310 --> 00:23:25.640
Just you wait! I’m on my way, Kaito!

00:23:27.480 --> 00:23:29.430
It looks like that is going to
be a fun journey,

00:23:30.150 --> 00:23:31.010
Kaito.

00:23:39.740 --> 00:23:41.700
It’s Mr. Puzzle!

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:45.120
Mr. Puzzle!
Mister!

00:23:45.120 --> 00:23:46.570
Oh, there you are!

00:23:47.080 --> 00:23:49.640
I solved the puzzle you left with me.

00:23:49.640 --> 00:23:50.700
Me, too!

00:23:51.000 --> 00:23:52.090
Same here!

00:23:52.340 --> 00:23:55.330
Yeah? You’re amazing, guys!

00:23:55.760 --> 00:23:58.880
Mister, where are the new puzzles?

00:23:58.880 --> 00:24:00.330
Hurry up! Hurry!

00:24:00.550 --> 00:24:02.220
I want one, too!

00:24:02.760 --> 00:24:04.390
Don’t be in such a rush.

00:24:08.690 --> 00:24:11.470
Let’s solve puzzles
together with the others.

00:24:14.480 --> 00:24:16.400
Okay, let’s get started!

00:24:20.780 --> 00:24:22.350
Puzzle time...

00:24:23.030 --> 00:24:24.950
Let’s begin!

00:24:27.940 --> 00:24:30.940
Art: Akeru Otsuki

00:24:27.940 --> 00:24:30.940
Let’s solve puzzles again! Fin
